  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>   <math><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is metallic oxide but  <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is non metallic oxide therefore  <math><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is basic but  <math><msub><mrow><mi>N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is acidic.<br > <math><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  In  <math><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi> </mi><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>N</mi><mi> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi> </mi><mi>F</mi></math>  are non metals but  <math><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mi> </mi><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></math>  is metal but  <math><mi>F</mi></math>  is non metal therefore  <math><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  is more covalent than  <math><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> <br > <math><mo>(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  In  <math><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  hydrogen bonding is absent but in  <math><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  hydrogen bonding is present therefore  <math><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math>  boils at lower temperature than  <math><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> <br > <math><mo>(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>)</mo></math>  Due to small size in N-N single bond l.p. - l.p. repulsion is more than P-P single bond therefore N-N single bond is weaker than the P-P single bond",
